    d("10:15:26 10:72:7 11:29:6 11:50:14 11:51:6 11:54:1 11:88:22 12:31:28 12:104:6 14:10:19", "Individually read the negative plus exception as one restriction. Turkish however/only or başka ... değil already expresses the combined force. Retain the context-only negative surface rather than introduce a second negation that changes the scope.", True)
    d("10:18:2 10:106:3", "Retain the Turkish bırakıp replacement frame for min duni with its accusative Allah'ı; no second source suffix is required in that chosen verbal paraphrase.", True)
    p("10:21", "plotted-content", [("kur",22),("duğ",21),("unuz tuzakları",22)], "Ma tamkuruna is what you plot. Restore the Turkish relative nominalization and the active plotting action rather than copying a possessed noun hilelerinizi at both source entries.")
    d("10:21:21", "Expose the relative content of the plots being recorded; tuzak kurmak retains the lexical plotting meaning.")
    p("10:27", "no-defender", [("hiçbir ",13),("koruyucu",14)], "Min asimin under negation denotes any defender. Restore a defender noun rather than an unattached future participle kurtaracak.")
    d("10:27:13", "Restore the unrestricted indefinite defender in the negative clause.")
    p("10:37", "fabrication-nominal", [("uydurul",6),("ma",5),("sı",6)], "An yuftara is the nominal content being denied of the Quran, not simply an adjective uydurulmuş. Restore uydurulması; the preceding negative copula governs this proposition.")
    p("10:37", "fabrication-impossibility", [("ve ",1),("mümkün",2),(" değil",1),("dir",2)], "Wa-ma kana ... an yuftara denies the possibility of fabrication. The nominal complement needs the whole Turkish modal frame mümkün değildir, not the ungrammatical uydurulması değildir.")
